# Build context for the self-hosting image (SELF_HOSTING.md §4.7).
#
# The list is short on purpose: everything kept here is either needed by
# `pnpm build`, or harmless. Everything excluded is either rebuildable
# (node_modules, .next), or must never enter an image at all (secrets), or is
# development-only material that would only make the context larger
# (tests, evidence, frozen reference material).

# --- rebuildable ----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
out
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- never in an image ----------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY: .env.local and .env.deploy.secrets in a developer's checkout hold the
# real ENCRYPTION_KEY / HASH_PEPPER and provider keys. `COPY . .` would bake them
# into a layer, and no later stage can un-bake a layer. Values reach the running
# container from the operator's environment (docker-compose.yml `env_file`),
# never from the build context.
.env
.env.*
.secrets/
client_secret_*.json
*.pem
.vercel/

# --- development-only material -------------------------------------------
tests/
playwright.config.ts
test-results/
playwright-report/
evidence/
docs-internal/
spec/
reference-landing/
.github/
# Runtime artifact of `pnpm dev` (the dev OTP log) — not input to a build.
.runtime/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- version control ------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
